{
  "_comment_intro": [
    "CREATE: COMMERCE — VILLAGE CONFIG",
    "Controls which village commerce profiles exist and which villages use them.",
    "",
    "HOW PROFILES WORK:",
    "  Each village is assigned one profile at world generation.",
    "  The profile determines which item categories the depot accepts,",
    "  which it accepts at a bonus rate, and which it refuses entirely.",
    "",
    "  'accepts'       : item tags or item IDs this village will buy.",
    "  'bonus_accepts' : items bought at 1.5x the normal payout (village speciality).",
    "  'refuses'       : items this village will NOT buy even if in a tag it accepts.",
    "                    Use this to remove one item from a broad accepted tag.",
    "",
    "HOW TO ADD A CUSTOM PROFILE:",
    "  1. Copy an existing profile block below.",
    "  2. Give it a new unique name (lowercase, underscores only).",
    "  3. Add it to the 'profile_weights' section with a weight value.",
    "  4. It will be randomly assigned to villages at generation.",
    "  Optionally, add its name to biome_overrides to force it in specific biomes.",
    "",
    "HOW TO FORCE A SPECIFIC VILLAGE TO USE A PROFILE:",
    "  1. Find the village's UUID (shown in the Trade Terminal detail view,",
    "     or enable debug.log_lectern_spawns in server.toml to see it in the log).",
    "  2. Add the UUID and profile name to village_overrides below.",
    "",
    "ITEM TAG FORMAT:",
    "  Use standard Minecraft tag IDs with a '#' prefix: '#minecraft:crops'",
    "  Use full item IDs without '#' for specific items: 'minecraft:wheat'",
    "  Modded items and tags work the same way: '#somefoodmod:foods'"
  ],

  "_comment_profile_weights": [
    "How likely each profile is to be assigned to a new village.",
    "Higher number = more common. All weights are relative to each other.",
    "Example: farming_settlement at 30 and military_garrison at 5 means",
    "farming settlements are 6x more common than garrisons.",
    "Weights are only used when biome_overrides does not apply."
  ],
  "profile_weights": {
    "farming_settlement": 30,
    "frontier_outpost":   15,
